# Build context for the seven service images (docker-compose.yml builds them all from the repository root).
#
# Allowlist: send src/ and nothing else, then drop what src/ must not contribute. Everything outside src/ -
# docs, tests, ui/, k8s/, infrastructure/, local scratch files, the stray .audit-base-worktree/ mirror, .env -
# stays out without being listed, so a new top-level folder cannot bloat or leak into the context (docker-ci DC-10).
# The Dockerfile itself is always sent, whatever this file says.
*
!src/

# Build output and local tooling state
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/node_modules/
**/.vs/
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/TestResults/
**/logs/
**/*.user
**/*.suo

# Dead client folder: zero tracked files, only a local node_modules/ and .next/
src/ClientApp/

# Local-only settings. The Web SDK publishes every appsettings*.json, so without this line a developer's
# appsettings.Development.Local.json - the file that exists to hold local secrets - is baked into the image
# (docker-ci DC-50: it was, in three images).
**/appsettings.*.Local.json
**/*.Local.json

# Documentation and agent notes are never needed to build
**/*.md
